# Upload hoisting (26 Nov): a guest-memory upload that no GPU work recorded so far in the submission reads goes into a
# second command buffer submitted before the main one, instead of ending the current render pass and adding two
# barriers. In busy scenes ~235 uploads a frame (vertex data the game rewrites each frame) split the passes (~1,460
# render passes, 8.5 ms of GPU upload time). Reads are tracked per 4 KB page from MemorySync::Request. Per-frame log
# line: "uploads moved ahead, in place". BOTS_GFX_HOIST_UPLOADS=0 turns it off (A/B).
